    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d24">

                <pb facs="0139" n="43" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg43"/>

                <head>No. 24.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Clapp
                        to Mr. Hunter.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United
                                States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Buenos
                            Ayres</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1872-09-12"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">September</hi> 12, 1872</date>. (Received
                        October 22.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 21.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that no
                    perceptible change has taken place in the condition of affairs as respects the
                    difficulty between the Argentine Republic and Brazil. Reports as to the success
                    of the mission of General Mitre are conflicting.</p>
                <p>I stated in a former dispatch that a portion of the Grand Chaco, about which more
                    than any other matter this trouble with Brazil has arisen, is claimed by the
                    republic of Bolivia. Señor R. Cordona has lately arrived at this capital, as
                    special envoy from Bolivia, for the settlement of this question.</p>
                <p>* * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>DEXTER E. CLAPP.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
